FerrionOS change to base (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 20f7573b4dc011ea5267189185edc0b2f12bab0f with ferrion-boot-splash.patch, ferrion-lockdown.patch, ferrion-pty-hangup.patch, ferrion-live-disk-view.patch, ferrion-sigchld.patch, ferrion-signal-handle-perm.patch, ferrion-rand-seed.patch and ferrion-driver-null-namespace.patch applied (issue 7). A forked namespace can keep the right to create schemes when asked:
- a fork request whose list of names holds the entry `namespace:scheme-create` gives the new namespace the right to create schemes, if the handle that forks it has that right. Without the entry a fork drops the right, as before. A scheme name cannot contain `:`, so no scheme is taken for the entry.
- /etc/login_schemes.toml lists the entry for an account whose logins may create schemes; `login` and `orblogin` pass the list unchanged, and both run with init's handle, which has the right.

